Lay-What: The app starts faster because the code for editing, admin and issue actions now loads only when first used.
Lay-How: The actions you take after the first screen, such as editing a message or managing members, are fetched the first time you use them.
Lay-Why: Every visitor downloaded the code for all those actions at start even when only reading.
Tech-What: 48 spool-client writer, admin and issue methods move to utils/spool-client-lazy.mjs; spool-client.mjs keeps first-screen reads plus one async stub per name.
Tech-How: Each stub imports the lazy chunk on first call so callers' await is unchanged; the lazy module exports one name read as a member to avoid Nuxt auto-import collisions; initial-js-trims.test.mjs guards it.
